---
// /brands/heartland-appliance-repair/ — Luxury Wave L-3. Heartland (ORPHAN BRAND).
// NEW. Heartland ceased manufacturing appliances Oct 31, 2019. Chain: Heartland BOUGHT the Oval/Sweetheart/Julia/5000/6000/7000 lines FROM Elmira Stove Works in 1990 (not the reverse — Elmira is still independent today); then AGA Marvel ~2008 -> Middleby 2015 -> Composition Brands 2026
// (1989)->AGA Marvel(~2008)->Middleby(2015); heartlandapp.com -> marvelrefrigeration.com.
// Formerly retro/classic refrigerators, ranges, wood cookstoves (Classic 30"/36" fridges
// discontinued). ORPHAN framing: service EXISTING units, HONEST parts-sourcing reality
// (AGA Marvel warranty legacy + third-party sellers, parts DEGRADE), repair-if-sourceable-
// else-replace lean. Wood cookstoves NOT emphasized (SCAQMD). NO sourced failure. $89.
// Verified: Wikipedia AGA Rangemaster + guaranteedparts + marvelrefrigeration redirect.
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import BrandBranchesGrid from '../../components/BrandBranchesGrid.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, MAIN_PHONE_TEL } from '../../data/branches';
import { mergeCredentials } from '../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../lib/build-location-array';
import { OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA } from '../../data/business-hours';

const title = "Heartland Appliance Repair Los Angeles";
const description = "Heartland appliance repair across LA — servicing existing Heartland retro ranges and refrigerators. Heartland stopped manufacturing in 2019; we're honest about parts sourcing and repair-vs-replace. $89 diagnostic.";
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/heartland-appliance-repair/";

const faqs = [
  { q: "Is Heartland still making appliances?", a: "No — and this is the first thing to know before any Heartland repair. Heartland ceased manufacturing appliances on October 31, 2019. The brand had a long history (its roots trace back through Ontario stove-making and it bought several of its cooker lines from Elmira Stove Works in 1990 — Elmira is still trading independently today — and the brand itself later passed to AGA Marvel, then into the Middleby group, and with the rest of that residential portfolio into Composition Brands in February 2026), but it is no longer in production. Its former site now points to Marvel refrigeration under AGA Marvel. What that means practically: we service the Heartland appliances still installed in LA kitchens, but there are no new Heartland units being built, and parts support is legacy-only. We'll always be straight with you about what that means for your specific repair. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { q: "Can you still get parts for a Heartland?", a: "Sometimes — and this is the honest heart of a Heartland repair. Because Heartland is discontinued, parts are not freshly manufactured; they come from legacy warranty support through AGA Marvel and from third-party parts sellers who still stock Heartland components. That means availability varies part by part and degrades over time — some components are still sourceable, others are getting hard to find. Our techs check availability for the specific part your repair needs before recommending anything, because on an orphaned brand that's the deciding factor. If the part exists, we fit it and your Heartland keeps going; if it's genuinely unobtainable, we tell you honestly rather than chase a part that isn't coming." },
  { q: "My Heartland range or refrigerator stopped working — is it worth repairing?", a: "It depends entirely on whether the failed part is still sourceable, and we'll assess that at the diagnostic. Many Heartland faults are standard gas-and-element or refrigeration problems — an igniter, a valve, a thermostat, an oven element, or on a Classic retro refrigerator the compressor, fan, or defrost system — and where those parts are still obtainable, the repair is usually worth it because Heartland appliances were premium retro units. Where it tips toward replacement is when a needed part is no longer available at any reasonable source; on an orphaned brand, an unobtainable part can effectively total the appliance, and we won't pretend otherwise. Our $89 diagnostic gets you a clear, honest answer either way." },
  { q: "What Heartland appliances do you service?", a: "The Heartland appliances still in service in LA kitchens — primarily the retro/classic ranges and the Classic-series retro refrigerators (the 30-inch single-door and 36-inch double-door models, now discontinued). Behind the vintage styling these are gas or electric ranges and conventional-cooling refrigerators, so the service is standard: burners, igniters, valves, oven elements and thermostats on the ranges; compressor, evaporator fan, and defrost on the refrigerators. Heartland also historically built other retro cooking appliances; for anything outside standard gas, electric, and refrigeration work we'll advise honestly on scope and parts availability when you call with your model." },
  { q: "Who supports Heartland now?", a: "Legacy support runs through AGA Marvel, which absorbed the Heartland brand before Heartland wound down manufacturing, and through independent parts sellers who still carry Heartland components. There's no active Heartland factory producing new parts, so support is about sourcing from existing stock rather than fresh production. As an independent service company, we're not the manufacturer — what we bring is honest diagnosis, the ability to check real parts availability through the surviving channels, and a straight repair-versus-replace recommendation. On an orphaned brand, that honesty is the most valuable thing a repair company can offer." },
  { q: "How fast can you get to a Heartland in LA?", a: "The diagnostic visit is same-day in most cases across Los Angeles, the Westside, Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside — we answer the phone 24/7. The honest variable on a Heartland is parts: because the brand is discontinued, sourcing a specific component through the surviving legacy and third-party channels can take time, and occasionally a part isn't available at all. We'll tell you the real situation at the $89 diagnostic — whether the part is on hand, sourceable with a lead time, or genuinely unobtainable — so you can make a clear-eyed decision about repairing or replacing." }
];

const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [
  { "@type": "Service", "serviceType": "Heartland Appliance Repair", "provider": { "@id": canonical + "#org" }, "areaServed": [
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Los Angeles County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Orange County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Ventura County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Santa Barbara County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Bernardino County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Riverside County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Diego County" }
    ], "description": "Heartland appliance repair across Los Angeles and Southern California — servicing existing Heartland retro ranges and Classic-series refrigerators. Heartland ceased manufacturing in 2019; parts are legacy-only through AGA Marvel and third-party sellers, so service comes with honest parts-availability assessment and repair-versus-replace guidance. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": f.q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '') } })) },
  { "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [ { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Brands", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Heartland Appliance Repair", "item": canonical } ] }
] };

const wave46OrgSchema = mergeCredentials({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HomeAndConstructionBusiness',
  '@id': canonical + '#org',
  name: 'Same Day Appliance Repair',
  url: canonical,
  priceRange: '$$',
  openingHoursSpecification: OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA,
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Los Angeles County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Orange County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Ventura County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Santa Barbara County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Bernardino County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Riverside County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Diego County' }
  ],
  location: BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL
});
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Fragment slot="head-scripts">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(wave46OrgSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <div class="call-banner"><div class="wrap"><span>Heartland needs service? Same-day diagnostic across LA:</span><a href={`tel:${MAIN_PHONE_TEL}`} class="phone-lg">{MAIN_PHONE}</a></div></div>
  <ServiceHero
    section="brands"
    slug="heartland-appliance-repair"
    eyebrow={"Heartland Appliance Repair"}
    title={"Heartland Appliance Repair, Los Angeles & Southern California"}
    subtitle={description}
    heroImageTitle={"Heartland Retro Appliance Repair"}
  />

  <BrandBranchesGrid />
  <section class="trust-bar"><div class="wrap"><span>Licensed BHGS #A49573 · Insured</span><span>Same-day · 7 Southern California counties</span><span>$89 residential diagnostic · waived with repair</span></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Heartland — an honest word before you book</h2>
    <p>Heartland made premium retro ranges and refrigerators for years, and plenty of them are still in LA kitchens — but here's the fact that shapes every Heartland repair: Heartland stopped manufacturing appliances on October 31, 2019. The brand bought its Oval, Sweetheart and Julia cooker lines from Elmira Stove Works in 1990 (Elmira itself is still independent and trading), then passed to AGA Marvel, into the Middleby group, and on into Composition Brands with the rest of that portfolio in February 2026; its old site now points to Marvel refrigeration. There is no active Heartland factory building new units or new parts. So a Heartland repair isn't like repairing a brand you can still buy — it's about keeping an existing appliance running, and being honest about what that takes. That's exactly how we approach it. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair, BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410).</p>
    <p>The appliances themselves are straightforward under the retro styling — gas or electric ranges and conventional-cooling refrigerators — so the diagnosis is standard appliance work. The variable, and the whole conversation on an orphaned brand, is parts. We check real availability before recommending anything, because on a discontinued brand the deciding question isn't "can we fix it" but "can we still get the part." We'll give you that answer straight.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>The parts reality on a discontinued brand</h2>
    <p>This is the section that matters most, so we'll be plain. Because Heartland is no longer manufactured, its parts are not freshly produced. They come from two surviving sources: legacy warranty support through AGA Marvel, and third-party parts sellers who still stock Heartland components. That means availability varies part by part and degrades over time — some components are still sourceable, others are increasingly hard to find, and a few may be effectively gone.</p>
    <p>What our techs do about it is simple and honest: before we recommend a repair, we check whether the specific part your Heartland needs is actually available through the surviving channels. If it is, we fit a genuine part and your Heartland keeps going — and given these were premium appliances, that's usually well worth doing. If the part is genuinely unobtainable, we tell you that plainly rather than chase something that isn't coming, and we talk through replacement. On an orphaned brand, that upfront honesty is the most useful thing we can offer.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Heartland appliances we service</h2>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Classic retro refrigerators</h3><p>The Classic-series retro refrigerators (30-inch single-door, 36-inch double-door, now discontinued). Conventional cooling under a vintage cabinet — compressor, evaporator fan, defrost, start relay, door seal. Serviced where parts remain sourceable.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Heartland gas ranges</h3><p>Retro-styled gas ranges — oven igniter, gas valve, thermocouple, oven thermostat, burner components. Standard gas-oven service, subject to parts availability.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Heartland electric ranges</h3><p>Electric retro ranges — bake element, temperature sensor, thermostat, and calibration. Standard electric-oven service.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Diagnosis &amp; parts-availability check</h3><p>The most valuable service on an orphaned brand: a real diagnosis plus a genuine check of whether the needed part can still be sourced — before you commit to a repair.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Honest repair-vs-replace</h3><p>Where a part is available, repair usually wins on a premium retro appliance. Where it isn't, we say so and talk replacement — no chasing unobtainable parts.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Other Heartland cooking appliances</h3><p>For anything outside standard gas, electric, and refrigeration work we advise honestly on scope and parts availability when you call with your model.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Related retro &amp; refrigeration pages</h2>
    <ul class="related-links">
      <li><a href="/brands/elmira-stove-works-repair/">Elmira Stove Works repair Los Angeles</a> — an active retro maker (parts still produced)</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/big-chill-refrigerator-repair/">Big Chill retro appliance repair Los Angeles</a></li>
      <li><a href="/brands/marvel/">Marvel refrigeration repair Los Angeles</a> — the AGA Marvel successor brand</li>
      <li><a href="/services/refrigerator-repair/">All refrigerator repair in Los Angeles →</a></li>
      <li><a href="/services/oven-repair/">All oven &amp; range repair in Los Angeles →</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>Heartland repair, frequently asked</h2>{faqs.map(f => <details class="faq"><summary>{f.q}</summary><p set:html={f.a}></p></details>)}</div></section>

  <section id="book" class="cta-bottom"><div class="wrap"><h2>Heartland need service? Start with an honest diagnostic.</h2><p>Same-day across LA, the Westside, Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair — including a real parts-availability check.</p></div></section>
</Layout>

<style>
  body { color: var(--text); } .wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; } .wrap.narrow { max-width: 820px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.4rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 12px 0 20px; color: var(--black); } h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--black); } h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--black); } p { line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .call-banner { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 10px 0; } .call-banner .wrap { display:flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; } .call-banner .phone-lg { color:#fff; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .trust-bar { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 14px 0; } .trust-bar .wrap { display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .section { padding: 56px 0; } .section.alt { background: var(--gray); }
  .model-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px; } .model-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 20px; border-radius: 6px; }
  .related-links { list-style: none; padding: 0; } .related-links li { padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } .related-links a { color: var(--red); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; } .related-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .faq { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-radius: 4px; } .faq summary { font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px 0; } .faq p { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .cta-bottom { background: var(--black); color: #fff; padding: 48px 0; } .cta-bottom h2 { color: #fff; } .cta-bottom p { color: #c9c9c9; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; } h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; }  .trust-bar .wrap { gap: 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; } }
</style>
